      "definition": "added to a noun to make an adjective meaning having that quality, or full of it",
      "explanation": "It is also spelled **-ious** and **-eous** (*mystery*, *mysterious*; *courage*, *courageous*). A final **y** after a consonant becomes **i** (*glory*, *glorious*). Many **-ous** adjectives have no noun beside them in English (*enormous*, *obvious*).",
